==============================================================================
PROOF-ROUTE READING
==============================================================================
1. The span>14 leader can be a boundary one-far row with second-largest <=14;
   this is distinct from the KPS true-wide-base branch (second-largest >14).
2. The true-wide rows in the finite boxes are much lower than the boundary leaders,
   supporting the KPS Plat/Delta entanglement split.
3. The worst rows keep long near-consecutive packets plus a sparse scaffold.
   They have high additive energy / low sumset excess compared with random wide rows,
   so Freiman-GAP structure is the correct language for the direct p0 bound.
4. Delta-only framing loses the plateau/coverage coupling.  The exact predicate to
   prove is a wide-row sector-cover deficit: once span>14, no row can retain the
   consecutive state-word density needed to approach cap_k.
5. The squarefree profiles and shell_missing fields show why a one-scalar dyadic or
   shell-1 law is insufficient: the same shell carrier can sit in low or high p0
   depending on the additive scaffold and missed-sector word.
